# ── Raw harvest caches — regenerated by scripts/, never edited
#    by hand, and about 1 GB of the ~1.04 GB under data/.
#
# WHY THEY ARE NOT IN THE REPO. Each of these is the RAW pull
# from an exchange or broker feed. The site never reads them; it
# reads the small derived files a script writes from them. So
# they are reproducible by re-running the harvester named in the
# script header, and carrying them in git buys nothing but a
# clone that takes twenty minutes.
#
# GitHub hard-blocks any single file over 100 MB, and
# data/ib_5m/China.json alone is 265 MB — so this is not tidiness,
# it is the difference between a push that lands and one that is
# rejected outright.
#
# ANYTHING THE APP READS MUST NOT BE HERE. The rule is: if a file
# under views/ opens it, it stays tracked. membership_history.json
# is the one file that matches a pattern below and is still
# needed, so it is excepted by name.
data/ib_5m/
data/tw_history/
data/twse_t86/
data/msci_archive/
data/tip_news/
data/gimi_editions/
data/factsheets/
data/*_history.json
!data/membership_history.json
data/ib_bars*.json
data/tv_bars.json
data/tw_vintage_cache.json
data/tw_daily_turnover.json
data/*_cache.json
data/tw_float_*.json
data/yahoo_*_raw.json
